1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Landed in Australia on 1954 December 31 on board the Star Queen.  They lived in a little white cottage in the village of Happy Valley and later shifted to a farm at Dashwood's Gully in 1859, when he immediately set
2 CONC  to work to build a house and clear the land for a garden of fruit trees and vegetables.
2 CONT
2 CONT William lived on the old homestead for over 60 years; he was 87 when he died and his wife lived until she was 84.
2 CONT
2 CONT There were 9 children in the family--Sarah, William, Elizabeth, Japhet, James, Ellen, Samuel and Alice.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ship: http://www.theshipslist.com/ships/australia/starqueen1854.shtml
