1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Theodore Standar, 65
2 CONT PULLMAN Theodore Henry Standar, 65, a retired
2 CONT builder and Pullman resident for 60 years, died at
2 CONT Friday at Pullman Memorial Hospital.
2 CONT Standar retired from the building trade 10 years ago
2 CONT because of poor health. He had built several houses in
2 CONT the Pullman and Colton areas.
2 CONT Standar was bom July at Minneapolis, Minn.,
2 CONT to Alex and Bessie Standar. He came to Washington
2 CONT with his family in 1918 and moved to Pullman in 1920.
2 CONT He and Claudene Reisenauer were married April 15,
2 CONT 1941, at Colton. He farmed with his in the
2 CONT then began the building and carpentry trades.
2 CONT His wife died in 1974. Survivors include two sons. Tim
2 CONT of and Jerry of Uniontown; two daughters. Judy
2 CONT McMurray and Janet K. Cooper, both of Pullman; and
2 CONT three grandchildren.
2 CONT Graveside services will be held Monday at
2 CONT at the Pullman City Cemetery, with the Rev. J. Severyn
2 CONT Westbrook, pastor of Sacred Heart Catholic Church at
2 CONT Pullman, officiating. Kimball Funeral Home. of Pullman
2 CONT is in charge of arrangements.
