1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charles was the biological son of Charles A. and Amanda Sofia (Nystrom) Stander who were married June 12, 1895 in Chicago, Cook County, Illinois at the Salem Lutheran Church. Charles A. Stander was born in Motala, 
2 CONC Sweden and immigrated in about 1888. Amanda Sofia Nystrom was the daughter of Frithiof Nystrom and Fredrika Fahlstrom. She was born in Motala, Sweden on November 13, 1870 and immigrated in 1889. Amanda passed away on November 19, 
2 CONC 1917 at the Peoria State Hospital where she had been patient for approximately 12 years. Her burial on November 20, 1917 is at the Peoria State Hospital Cemetery .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1910, young Charles was living in Chicago as Charles Oberg, a nephew of Eric and Anna M. Oberg. Anna's maiden name was Nystrom. She was a sister to his mother Amanda (Nystrom) Stander.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eric Oberg's obituary lists Charles as a son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles married Johanna Rita Dineen on February 14, 1920 in Chicago.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biological siblings include:
2 CONT - Mae Caroline Stander born May 1, 1897 in Chicago, Illinois. "May Standard", age 12, was a boarder with the August and Amanda Johnson family in 1910 in Chicago. The Johnson family were on the same census page with the Stander fam
2 CONC ily in 1900. Mae married Edward T. Hawks in 1917.
2 CONT - Julia Standar Bivens born June 1899 or 1898
2 CONT - Olga Stander Schreiber born August 9, 1901
2 CONT - Ruth Mae Saabye Cornell, born Louise Stander on April 21, 1903. Ruth was adopted by Christian and Johanna Saabye of Washington Island, Door, Wisconsin in 1904.
