1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Biological parents were Charles A Stander and Amanda Nystrom. Amanda Sofia Nystrom was born November 13, 1870 in Motala, Sweden. She immigrated in 1889. She wed Charles A Stander on June 12, 1895 at Salem Lutheran 
2 CONC Church in Chicago. She passed on November 19, 1917 at the Peoria State Hospital where she was a patient for almost 12 years. She was buried in the cemetery there on November 20, 1917.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family fell on tough times and fell apart and the children were placed in different homes. In 1920 we see Julia residing with the Bivens family listed as a foster daughter. She would marry son Clarence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her biological siblings include
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Oberg memorial 225030734
2 CONT Mae Hawks memorial 225050369
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles, Julia and Mae can be found on the 1900 Census with their birth parents
2 CONT
2 CONT Biological siblings born after 1900
2 CONT
2 CONT Olga Schreiber memorial 225051128
2 CONT Ruth Cornell memorial 43714121
2 CONT
2 CONT The four eldest siblings clearly stay connected through the years. We see articles in the local newspapers of some of Julia's siblings visiting her over the years. Additionally, Julia lived the longest of the four eldest siblings 
2 CONC and she is mentioned in each of their obits posted to their memorials. The youngest sibling Ruth was adopted by a family residing on Washington Island Wisconsin. We located her adoption notice in the paper where we see she had bee
2 CONC n born Louise Stander daughter of Charles and Amanda Stander. Her family shared that Ruth knew only that she was born in Chicago to Swedish immigrants.
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT Julia Bivens (född Standar) was born on November 14 1898, in Chicago, Cook County, Illinois, United States.
2 CONT Her father Karl Alfred Standar was born on February 3 1869, in Rogberga, Jönköping.
2 CONT Her mother Amanda Sofia Florentina Nyström was born on November 13 1870, in Motala Mekaniska Werkstad, 
2 CONT Motala (E), Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT She had 3 sisters: Mae Caroline, Olga C and Ruth Mae.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband Clarence Ernest Bivens was born on September 24 1889, in Moro, Madison County, IL, United States, and they had 3 children: Clara Marie, Clifford Elwood and Arlene June.
2 CONT
2 CONT She lived at Moro, Illinois 62067, USA.
2 CONT She lived in 1930, at Moro, Madison, Illinois, United States.
2 CONT She lived in 1935, at Madison, Illinois, Madison, Illinois.
2 CONT She lived in 1940, at Moro, Moro Township, Madison, Illinois, United States, Moro, Moro Township, Madison, Illinois, United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT She passed away Circa April 1983, at age 84.
