1 NAME Jonas /Svensson Wåhlstrand/
2 GIVN Jonas
2 SURN Svensson Wåhlstrand
2 _MARNM Svensson Wåhlstrand
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 4 JUN 1747
2 PLAC Kullstugan
2 ADDR
3 CITY Dalhem
3 STAE Kalmar County
3 CTRY Sweden
1 BAPM
2 DATE 5 JUN 1747
2 ADDR
3 CITY Dalhem
3 STAE Kalmar County
3 CTRY Sweden
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1800
2 PLAC Sweden
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was Bailiff (''Befallningsman'' or ''Betjänt'') of Tyllinge for [http://www.geni.com/people/Baron-Sven-Johan-Duwall/6000000018924067437 Baron Sven Johan Duwall] (1746-1819). The baron was also godfather to Jonas
2 CONC ' son Sven. Jonas and his wife disappear from the household rolls about 1800, when a new bailiff took his place.
2 CONT
2 CONT Justin Swanström has suggested that Jonas might have been the baron's illegitimate half-brother, although the  evidence is circumstantial. There is a family tradition among some of Jonas' Wåhlstrand's descendants that their unname
2 CONC d ancestor was the illegitimate son of a Scottish nobleman. Taken together with the fact that Baron Sven Duwall was godfather to Jonas' son Sven, it is possible that there is a relationship but it is also possible that family trad
2 CONC ition has garbled the facts. It should be noted that it was relatively common for a prominent man or woman to stand as a godparent for the first child of important servants.
2 CONT
2 CONT The tradition of descent from a Scottish nobleman appears in modern generations of two different branches descended from [http://www.geni.com/people/Inga-Lena-Honette/6000000015982197118 Inga Honette] (1800-1870), a granddaughter 
2 CONC of Jonas Wåhlstrand and wife of [http://www.geni.com/people/Jonas-Svanstr%C3%B6m/6000000003827138794 Jonas Svanström]. The tradition implies that the Scottish nobleman was the father of the Svanström line, but the tradition does n
2 CONC ot fit the known facts for either Jonas Svanström or his father [http://www.geni.com/people/Petter-Cavat/6000000003827145169 Peter Cavat], but it does fit, broadly speaking, Jonas Wåhlstrand, who was connected to the Duwalls, a no
2 CONC ble family with roots in Scotland. In contrast, the family tradition is not known among the descendants of [http://www.geni.com/people/Sven-H%C3%B6ckert/6000000012361216358 Sven Höckert] (1785-1859), the son of Jonas Wåhlstrand.
2 CONT
2 CONT If Jonas was an illegitimate Duwall, his DNA should match some other members of the interrelated MacDowall and Duwall families, but it's not certain whether they do. The MacDowalls and MacDougalls are two distinct Scottish familie
2 CONC s with similar surnames. Sven Höckert's descendants belong to Haplogroup I1. This result does not match the majority of MacDougall families. Most MacDougalls belong to Haplogroup R1b, although there is one known I1 result (2015). 
2 CONC Results for members of the MacDowell family are not being made public at this time (2015). The reason for this unusual secrecy is unknown, but it is rumored that results show a major break in the MacDowall line. 
2 CONT
